summary:
- topic: FY2025 Budget
  text: The board and superintendent expressed gratitude to South Portland voters
    for passing the school budget referendum with a significant 22% margin of support.
- topic: Personnel
  text: The retirement of Kelly Perkins, a long-serving and beloved clerk at Brown
    Elementary School, was announced and met with fond farewells from board members.
- topic: Personnel
  text: The board unanimously approved the hiring of Ashley Peterson as a new third-grade
    teacher for Kaler Elementary School.
- topic: Contracts
  text: Following an executive session, the board voted to approve a tentative agreement
    with the South Portland Education Support Professionals Association (SPESPA) to
    resolve an apprentice dispute.
- topic: Superintendent Search
  text: After a second executive session for a confidential personnel matter, the
    board voted to initiate a search for an interim superintendent.
- topic: Superintendent Search
  text: The board voted to engage the Maine School Management Association (MSMA) to
    assist in the search for an interim superintendent.
- topic: Superintendent Search
  text: A motion was passed to authorize the board chair and legal counsel to negotiate
    a separation agreement with Superintendent Metheny, contingent upon a successful
    interim superintendent search.
- topic: Superintendent Search
  text: Board members discussed the importance of leadership stability, expressing
    openness to having an interim superintendent serve for the entire school year
    to minimize transitions.
